{"content":[{"c":["AARONITES*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Collective name for the priests who descended from Aaron through his sons Eleazar and Ithamar. The term is used twice in the ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," to refer to the 3,700 men who supported David against Saul (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.12.27","r":"1Chr.12.27","rawR":"1Chr.12.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.12.27","value":"1Chr.12.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 12:27"},") and of whom Zadok later became leader (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.17","r":"1Chr.27.17","rawR":"1Chr.27.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.17","value":"1Chr.27.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:17"},"). Both “house of Aaron” (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.115.10,12","r":"Ps.115.10,12","rawR":"Ps.115.10,12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.115.10,12","value":"Ps.115.10,12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 115:10, 12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.118.3","r":"Ps.118.3","rawR":"Ps.118.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.118.3","value":"Ps.118.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"118:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.135.19","r":"Ps.135.19","rawR":"Ps.135.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.135.19","value":"Ps.135.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"135:19"},") and “Aaron” (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.17","r":"1Chr.27.17","rawR":"1Chr.27.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.17","value":"1Chr.27.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:17"},", ",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},") are used to refer to the Aaronites."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Aaron_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Aaron_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Aaron_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Aaron"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Aaronites","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 12:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.12.27","raw